  "description": "SETVUM crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C52 H54 Cr2 Dy3 N1 O27. From the CIF bond table, Dy01 (Dy) has 9 O neighbors; Dy02 (Dy) has 9 O neighbors; Dy03 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Cr04 (Cr) has 6 O neighbors; Cr05 (Cr) has 6 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 9 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.412-4.013 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 102.38-110.94°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C52H54Cr2Dy3NO27. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 6 OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 1 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 3 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)). Article name explicitly identifies Cr(III), Dy(III).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
